  {
   "key": "func MorningNotificationScheduler.deliverWakeTriggeredPushIfAppropriate(sleepEnd:)",
   "hash": "3f4d9d09605470e2",
   "does": "For Smart delivery with notifications enabled and authorized (settings read again after the authorization await), if the sleep end is a morning wake and the day's push can be claimed, builds a payload from the archive (with whether iOS hides previews on the locked screen) and delivers it immediately, recording whether it carries this morning's reading. A replacement claim (the first push went out before the night was scored) is sent only when the payload now carries the reading; otherwise the day is left open and nothing is sent.",
   "entry": "HealthKit sleep observer update handler (HealthKitManager+SleepTrends.swift:482).",
   "calls": [
    "Emuqu/Sources/Services/MorningNotificationScheduler.swift::func MorningNotificationScheduler.sendsWakePush(_:)",
    "ext:UNUserNotificationCenter.notificationSettings",
    "Emuqu/Sources/Services/MorningNotificationScheduler.swift::func MorningNotificationScheduler.isMorningWake(_:schedule:)",
